 "result_text": "`github checkout-prs` no longer leaves HEAD on whichever PR branch it created last. I haven't run the code or any tests.\n\n- **Fix:** `checkout_github_prs` in `git_machete/client.py` now records the current branch before it starts. If exactly one PR was checked out, it switches to that PR's head branch, as before. In every other case it switches back to the branch you started on. If HEAD was detached to begin with, nothing is restored.\n- **Docs:** I changed the wording to \"If only one PR has been checked out, then switch\u2026\" in `docs/source/cli_help/github.rst` and `git_machete/docs.py`. A grep for the old wording found nothing left elsewhere in the repo.\n- **Tests:** The issue asks for regression tests, but your instructions said not to add or modify tests, so I didn't write any.\n\nFor the `--by=amalota` example in the issue, HEAD would now stay on `develop`.",
